{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"coed-defectible-muskox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nCurrent macOS CI records 25.3s in the Jira capability retry test, 15.0s in the dependency-audit infrastructure retry test, and 15.8s in the stale-binding 500 test. The first two patch time.sleep after functions captured it in default arguments; the third exercises the retry policy without replacing its backoff. Runtime A/B: dependency audit 15.007s with real sleeps versus 0.000s with an injected sleeper; stale-binding 15.8s in CI versus 1.30s with no-op backoff. Assertions and attempt counts were unchanged.\n\n## Plan\nLate-bind or explicitly inject sleepers at the two production seams, and make the three unit tests pass no-op/recording sleepers. Preserve production retry counts, schedules, exception behavior, and all assertions. Add a guard that fails if these unit tests call real time.sleep.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Jira capability retry still proves six searches and records five 5-second logical delays without sleeping.\n- [ ] Dependency audit still proves three attempts and logical 5s/10s delays without sleeping.\n- [ ] The stale-binding 500 test still proves retry exhaustion/propagation without wall-clock backoff.\n- [ ] Production retry defaults and behavior are unchanged.\n- [ ] Focused tests fail if real time.sleep is reached.","id":"5ea3-76e5-480a-4464","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["ci","performance","tests"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Unit tests execute production retry sleeps through import-bound defaults"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786598831270121001,"uuid":"4302ffe2-a68a-4c14-af57-80f64ad7a3eb"}